.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt LIBTZFSD 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tzfsd_connect ,
.Nm tzfsd_adopt ,
.Nm tzfsd_close ,
.Nm tzfsd_request ,
.Nm tzfsd_request_quota ,
.Nm tzfsd_release ,
.Nm tzfsd_destroy ,
.Nm tzfsd_ping ,
.Nm tzfsd_begin_session ,
.Nm tzfsd_mount_dir
.Nd client interface to the tzfsd storage daemon
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libtzfsd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In tzfsd.h
.Ft struct tzfsd_client *
.Fn tzfsd_connect "void"
.Ft struct tzfsd_client *
.Fn tzfsd_adopt "int channel_fd"
.Ft void
.Fn tzfsd_close "struct tzfsd_client *c"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_request "struct tzfsd_client *c" "const struct tzfsd_req *req" "struct tzfsd_grant *out"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_request_quota "struct tzfsd_client *c" "const struct tzfsd_req *req" "uint64_t quota" "struct tzfsd_grant *out"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_release "struct tzfsd_client *c" "const char *dataset"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_destroy "struct tzfsd_client *c" "const char *dataset" "uint32_t lifetime"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_ping "struct tzfsd_client *c"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_begin_session "struct tzfsd_client *c" "const char *session"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_mount_dir "int handle_fd" "int rdonly"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm libtzfsd
is the client library for
.Xr tzfsd 8 ,
the
.Sy [TZFS]
storage daemon.
A consumer asks
.Xr tzfsd 8
for storage of a given lifetime and receives a rights-limited
TrustedZFS dataset handle, which it then drives with the
.Xr trustedzfs 3
verb interface.
This library only
.Em obtains
the handle; it does not duplicate the verb surface.
Its symbols use the
.Sy tzfsd_
prefix so a program may link both this library and
.Xr trustedzfs 3
without collision.
.Pp
.Xr tzfsd 8
is a socket-free capability-plane service: there is no daemon socket to connect
and no channel descriptor to thread through the calls.
A claim is reached by name through the well-known service
.Dq Li system.Filesystem ,
and every claim is created inside a namespace derived from the caller's own
unforgeable channel label, so a caller can only ever name storage in its own
subtree.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_connect
opens a channel to
.Xr tzfsd 8
by name
.Pq internally Fn service_open "system.Filesystem"
and returns an opaque client handle the caller owns and must
.Fn tzfsd_close ,
or
.Dv NULL
with
.Va errno
set.
.Fn tzfsd_adopt
instead wraps an already-held storage channel descriptor
.Pq for example one Xr serviced 8 delivered pre-scoped to a claim
as a client handle; it consumes
.Fa channel_fd
on success and returns a handle, or
.Dv NULL
with
.Va errno
set.
.Fn tzfsd_close
releases a client handle and its channel.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_request
asks for a handle described by
.Fa req :
.Bl -tag -width ".Va owner_uid" -offset indent
.It Va dataset
opaque single-component claim key within the caller's own namespace.
.It Va rights
the
.Dv ZH_*
mask to grant; the returned handle carries no more than these.
.It Va flags
.Dv ZHF_*
.Pq Dv ZHF_SUBTREE ,
0 for the common case.
.It Va lifetime
one of
.Dv TZFSD_PERSISTENT ,
.Dv TZFSD_CACHE ,
.Dv TZFSD_BOOT ,
or
.Dv TZFSD_LEASE .
.It Va owner_uid , Va owner_gid
if
.Va owner_uid
is nonzero, the dataset root is
.Xr chown 2 Ns 'd
to this owner at mint time so the service can write its own storage.
.El
.Pp
On success it returns 0 and fills
.Fa out ,
whose
.Va handle_fd
the caller owns and must
.Xr close 2 ,
and whose
.Va dataset
holds the resolved dataset name for audit.
.Fn tzfsd_request_quota
is
.Fn tzfsd_request
with an explicit per-claim
.Sy refquota
ceiling of
.Fa quota
bytes; 0 selects the daemon's configured default
.Pq see Va default_refquota in Xr tzfs.conf 5 ,
and a value below the daemon's floor is rejected with
.Er EINVAL .
.Fn tzfsd_request
is exactly this with
.Fa quota
== 0.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_release
destroys the caller's own
.Dv TZFSD_LEASE
claim previously granted under
.Fa dataset .
It is idempotent: a missing claim is success.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_destroy
reclaims a
.Dv TZFSD_PERSISTENT
or
.Dv TZFSD_CACHE
claim previously granted under
.Fa dataset ,
freeing its pool space;
.Fa lifetime
must be
.Dv TZFSD_PERSISTENT
or
.Dv TZFSD_CACHE .
Unlike
.Fn tzfsd_release
it is
.Em not
idempotent: an absent claim returns -1 with
.Va errno
set to
.Er ENOENT ,
so a caller can distinguish a real reclaim from a no-op.
The claim is resolved under the caller's own label-derived namespace, so no
other label's claim can be named.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_ping
verifies the daemon is answering.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_begin_session
begins or resumes one service-manager lease generation named by
.Fa session ,
reconciling the ephemeral lease datasets against it.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_mount_dir
mounts a granted handle and returns a directory descriptor for its root,
selecting a read-only mount when
.Fa rdonly
is nonzero.
It is a thin wrapper over
.Xr tzfs_mount 3
and requires the handle to carry
.Dv ZH_MOUNT .
.Pp
Programs that acquire storage through their manifest, rather than driving
.Xr tzfsd 8
directly, use the socket-free
.Fn service_storage_open ,
.Fn service_storage_open_quota ,
.Fn service_storage_destroy ,
and
.Fn service_storage_list
family in
.Xr libservice 3 ,
which speaks the same
.Dq Li system.Filesystem
protocol.
Enumeration of a caller's own claims is provided there
.Pq Fn service_storage_list ;
this library does not expose a list call.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn tzfsd_connect
and
.Fn tzfsd_adopt
return a client handle, or
.Dv NULL
with
.Va errno
set.
.Fn tzfsd_mount_dir
returns a descriptor, or -1 with
.Va errno
set.
The remaining functions return 0 on success or -1 with
.Va errno
set to the daemon-reported error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr trustedzfs 3 ,
.Xr tzfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr tzfsctl 8 ,
.Xr tzfsd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
